From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:04:27 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] internal/syscall/windows: pass lpBytesReturned when setting a reparse point

Root.Symlink creates a link by opening the new file and setting a reparse
point on it with DeviceIoControl. CL 660635 (Go 1.25) wrote that call with a
null lpBytesReturned and a null lpOverlapped, a pair the documentation
forbids. Windows 7 writes the byte count through the pointer without looking
and the process dies. Later Windows do not, or Go 1.25 and 1.26 could not
have created a symlink there.

	os.Root.Symlink  ->  DeviceIoControl(FSCTL_SET_REPARSE_POINT, ...)
	                 ->  lpBytesReturned is null
	                 ->  Windows 7 writes the count to address 0
	                 ->  Exception 0xc0000005, the process is gone

Pass a variable for the count, as every other DeviceIoControl call in the
tree already does. This is upstream's own fix, CL 744282 (Go 1.27), which was
not backported to Go 1.26. Nothing is gated, because the pointer is correct on
every Windows.

The symlink tests in os cover the call. Measured on Windows 7 RTM, where
TestSymlink took the whole os test binary down with the exception above, and
where the fixed binary runs past it.

diff --git a/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go b/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go
index f90ca93b..7d3556ab 100644
--- a/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go
+++ b/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go
@@ -915,6 +915,7 @@ func symlinkat(oldname string, newdirfd syscall.Handle, newname string, flags Sy
 	namebuf := rdbbuf[bufferSize:]
 	copy(namebuf, unsafe.String((*byte)(unsafe.Pointer(&oldnameu16[0])), 2*len(oldnameu16)))
 
+	var bytesReturned uint32
 	err = syscall.DeviceIoControl(
 		h,
 		FSCTL_SET_REPARSE_POINT,
@@ -922,7 +923,7 @@ func symlinkat(oldname string, newdirfd syscall.Handle, newname string, flags Sy
 		uint32(len(rdbbuf)),
 		nil,
 		0,
-		nil,
+		&bytesReturned,
 		nil)
 	if err != nil {
 		// Creating the symlink has failed, so try to remove the file.
